      "id": "sec-ar-4",
      "type": "reflection",
      "body": "The philosophy of modern architecture is the philosophy of total erasure. When a building fails to meet the current thermal efficiency standards or the floor-area ratio required by speculative capital, it is not repaired; it is declared economically obsolete, crushed into pulverized aggregate, and carted away to municipal landfills to make room for four-sided boxes of curtain-wall glass and extruded aluminium. We have unlearned the ancient, humble understanding that an architecture that cannot be repaired by ordinary hands is not an achievement of civilization, but a prison manufactured for consumption."
